<article class="env-theorem" id="0255">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0255">Theorem <span data-tag="0255">41.10.1</span>.</a> Let $Y$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism which is locally of finite type. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. The set of points in $X$ where $\mathcal{F}$ is flat over $Y$ is an open set. In particular the set of points where $f$ is flat is open in $X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      See More on Morphisms, Theorem <a href="/tag/0399" data-tag="0399">37.15.1</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>